+# ::a1 The office coffee machine should go
+
+::a2 I would like to propose that we get rid of the capsule machine in the kitchen and switch to a kettle and a French press. ::a3 The machine costs us around forty euros a month in capsules alone. ::a4 It breaks roughly twice a year, and every repair leaves us without coffee for a week. ::a5 The capsules are not recyclable in any practical sense, whatever the packaging says. ::a6 And the coffee it produces is, to be blunt, not very good.
+
+::a7 A kettle and a press would cost us maybe sixty euros once, take up less space, and be impossible to break in any interesting way. ::a8 The obvious objection is that it takes three minutes longer in the morning. ::a9 I think that is a price worth paying. ::a10 If anyone disagrees, now would be the time to say so.
